  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Canada-India Migration Initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aligned with the objectives of the Global Compact for Safe, Orderly and Regular Migration (GCM), there is a call for a whole-of government approach to ensure &#x201C;horizontal and vertical policy coherence across all sectors and levels of government,&#x201D; as well as a whole-of society approach that includes local communities in migration governance. These approaches will be pursued in conjunction with respect for human rights, gender equality, and accessibility, regardless of migration status and across all stages of the migration cycle. Therefore, with IOM&#x2019;s ongoing work on international labour mobility and migration opportunities for aspiring Indian migrants through strengthened migration management frameworks, and promotion of safe, orderly, and regular migration to Canada, IOM reciprocated the interest and highlighted its strengths, capacity, and stakeholder networks (particularly involving the State Governments) to contribute to interventions aligned with the Government of Canada&#x2019;s migration and humanitarian priorities through the following objectives:&#x2022;Advancement of capacity building efforts&#x2022;Increasing the development and exchange of migration-related information and expertise&#x2022;Improving migration management systems&#x2022;Preventing misinformation through communication campaigns</narrative>
  </description>
